{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/975185-do-i-really-need-it","id":975185,"title":"Do I really NEED it?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-23T13:01:05-07:00","id":975185,"title":"Do I really NEED it?","content":"Currently I already own all of the first edition CofD books as well as Beast and WtF 2nd ed. Since I have the 1st edition core book and the god machine rules updates along with the fact the new core line books are self contained with 2nd ed rules, do I really need to puck up the 2nd ed CofD corr book? I've been considering it, but I wasn't certain how much it would benefit me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5610-aslan751","name":"aslan751","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5610_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T13:15:53-07:00","id":975194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aslan751</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/975185-do-i-really-need-it#post975185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Currently I already own all of the first edition CofD books as well as Beast and WtF 2nd ed. Since I have the 1st edition core book and the god machine rules updates along with the fact the new core line books are self contained with 2nd ed rules, do I really need to puck up the 2nd ed CofD corr book? I've been considering it, but I wasn't certain how much it would benefit me.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Depends. Do you want:<br /> <br /> -Monster-of-the-week generation rules?<br /> <br /> -Investigation system?<br /> <br /> -The long-vanished Fate rules, now present as an optional sidebar?<br /> <br /> If your answer is &quot;yes&quot; to any of these questions, you can't go wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T13:19:32-07:00","id":975198,"title":"","content":"Need? No.<br /> <br /> Worth it? Depends, but probably.<br /> <br /> Besides condensing down to one book anyway, but CofD 2e core introduces a number of new subsystems no in the GMCRU and not always included in the supernatural core rule books (mostly because they were developed after those books). The new Crafting (not exactly what it sounds when people think about it, and not just about the Craft Skill), Investigation (also not just about the Investigation Skill),and Chase rules are all very useful additions to the ST toolkit for expanded in-depth rules for things other than combat and social maneuvering when you want them to be more than a simple or extended roll off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T13:31:46-07:00","id":975206,"title":"","content":"You definitely don't need it. You can absolutely play without it and you'll get by just fine. However, there are some advantages to getting the 2e core book that I considered well worth it. Your mileage may vary.<br /> <br /> The first, and most obvious is that it's the most complete version of the 2e core rules available. The God-Machine chronicle rrequires cross-referencing with the 1e core book, and the core books for other lines contain trunkated versions of the core rules, shortened to fit the minimum needed to play the game within a single chapter.<br /> <br /> Additionally, the 2e core book contains some optional rules not found in any other book. They are optional, so you don't NEED them, but they might improve your game. These optional rules include a system for crafting equipment, including non-physical equipment like plans and organizations (in my opinion, the best crafting system I've seen in an RPG), a system for running chase scenes which makes them much more dynamic and interesting than the standard footchase action, and a system for running Investigations which I don't use personally, but many people like and praise. There's also a system for creating custom monsters, kind of like the one from 1e Hunter.<br /> <br /> I like to look at the 2e &quot;core book&quot; as more of a supplemental blue book than a true core. It's not needed to play the game, but it has a lot of great options for expanding upon the core rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T13:48:06-07:00","id":975216,"title":"","content":"Honestly I'd say avoid it unless you play mortal games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T13:52:46-07:00","id":975220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/975185-do-i-really-need-it?p=975216#post975216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly I'd say avoid it unless you play mortal games.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually enjoy running mortal games, but it isn't something I would do constantly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5610-aslan751","name":"aslan751","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5610_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T14:01:04-07:00","id":975222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aslan751</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/975185-do-i-really-need-it?p=975220#post975220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually enjoy running mortal games, but it isn't something I would do constantly.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's mainly because the Horror builder is good for making like, 'monster of the week' monsters that aren't necessarily linked to a line. But if you have Werewolf, which you said you did, you have access to a wide variety of monster making stuff.<br /> <br /> I would suggest holding off until Hurt Locker. The Promethean pdf also has some monster-crafting mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T14:01:33-07:00","id":975223,"title":"","content":"Can I get a page number on that Fate Sidebar?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T14:31:23-07:00","id":975234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monghani</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/975185-do-i-really-need-it?p=975223#post975223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can I get a page number on that Fate Sidebar?</div> </div> </div> </div>177. It's almost identical to the drawback of the Destiny Merit from Mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T16:36:36-07:00","id":975268,"title":"","content":"You probably don't need it, but I'm happy I bought it slash happy that I made my parents buy it for my birthday a few years ago.<br /> <br /> I love the investigation rules, and the changes to what was the Morality system, breaking points, etc. I also love the equipment sections Char is talking about. Honestly--and this is just for me--everything I wanted in first edition they put into second. And I'm not saying that because I write for the company, I didn't when this book came out and when I made my parents buy it for me. It's great. Seriously great.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T16:43:44-07:00","id":975272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hm8453a</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/975185-do-i-really-need-it?p=975268#post975268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You probably don't need it, but I'm happy I bought it slash happy that I made my parents buy it for my birthday a few years ago.<br /> <br /> I love the investigation rules, and the changes to what was the Morality system, breaking points, etc. I also love the equipment sections Char is talking about. Honestly--and this is just for me--everything I wanted in first edition they put into second. And I'm not saying that because I write for the company, I didn't when this book came out and when I made my parents buy it for me. It's great. Seriously great.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think aslyn is referring to the book titled <i>Chronicles of Darkness</i>, not ChroD2e in general, since they said they have Beast, Werewolf 2e, and the GMC rules update.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T17:28:11-07:00","id":975300,"title":"","content":"Honestly, if you just have the 2E Rules Update, the actual God Machine Chronicle (in the back) is a pretty neat thing to have too and full of plot hooks. But definitely not a &quot;necessary&quot; purchase if you're rationing out your funds.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T05:22:57-07:00","id":975477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/975185-do-i-really-need-it?p=975272#post975272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think aslyn is referring to the book titled <i>Chronicles of Darkness</i>, not ChroD2e in general, since they said they have Beast, Werewolf 2e, and the GMC rules update.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I really like the 2nd edition rules changes specifically with things like conditions and tilts, but I just didn't know how much extra good stuff might be in the &quot;core&quot; book.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenesis</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly, if you just have the 2E Rules Update, the actual God Machine Chronicle (in the back) is a pretty neat thing to have too and full of plot hooks. But definitely not a &quot;necessary&quot; purchase if you're rationing out your funds.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's kind of what I've been wondering about. I'm not huge on the GodMachine, but if there are other things in the book I don't have then it might be worth it.<br /> <br /> @all. Thanks for all the great advice so far!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5610-aslan751","name":"aslan751","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5610_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T08:23:18-07:00","id":975525,"title":"","content":"<img src=\"http://s2.quickmeme.com/img/b5/b5b751e1332e32685063387b50636502158b2157ec78f4cbf733248c79cac4ad.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Sorry. I have no self control.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/